1. https://console.cloud.google.com/
2. Select a Project / Create new project.
3. Create a billing account and link it to the project.
3. GOTO API / Service Details -> Cloud Build API - Enable this

4. Install Google Cloud SDK - https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install

5. GCP Commands
    gcloud auth login - authenticate with your google account
    gcloud init - initialize the gcloud environment
    gcloud config set project < YOUR_PROJECT_ID - GCP project ID > - set the project for gcloud commands
      ex: gcloud config set project fine - tractor - 414013
    gcloud services enable run.googleapis.com
    gcloud services enable cloudbuild.googleapis.com

6. Create a Dockerfile in the root of your project with the following content:

Filename: Dockerfile
    FROM eclipse - temurin: 21 - jre - alpine
WORKDIR / app
    COPY target / springboot - sample - 1.0 - SNAPSHOT.jar app.jar
ENTRYPOINT["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]

7. docker build - t gcr.io / YOUR_PROJECT_ID / springboot - app.
    ex: docker build - t gcr.io / fine - tractor - 414013 / springboot - app.
        Note: Make sure to run this command from the root of your project where the Dockerfile is located. 
   The docker has to be installed on your machine to run this command.
   the docker hast to be started before running this command.
   -> docker push gcr.io / fine - tractor - 414013 / springboot - app
    -> docker tag springboot - app asia - south1 - docker.pkg.dev / fine - tractor - 414013 / my - repo / springboot - app

8. gcloud run deploy springboot - app--image gcr.io / fine - tractor - 414013 / springboot - app--platform managed--region asia - south1--allow - unauthenticated
  After this step we will get a URL where our application is deployed and we can access it from there.



